<p dir="auto">A working, demonstrable Security Operations Center pipeline that turns <strong>kernel-level eBPF telemetry</strong>
into <strong>MITRE ATT&amp;CK-mapped detections</strong>, <strong>traces lateral movement across hosts</strong>, and <strong>autonomously
contains attacks</strong> (freezes process trees, isolates hosts, blocks IPs). Everything is visible on a
live investigation dashboard.</p>
<p dir="auto"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://github.com/Poojasonwane08/ebpf-autonomous-soc/blob/main/ebpf-threat-hunting-soc/docs/images/dashboard.png"><img src="https://github.com/Poojasonwane08/ebpf-autonomous-soc/raw/main/ebpf-threat-hunting-soc/docs/images/dashboard.png" alt="Dashboard" style="max-width: 100%;"></a></p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Runs on Windows.</strong> eBPF needs a Linux kernel, so by default the project uses a <strong>sensor simulator</strong>
that emits the <em>exact JSON format of Cilium Tetragon</em> for a fleet of 5 virtual Linux servers.
The same pipeline consumes <strong>real Tetragon eBPF events</strong> on a Linux machine (see
<a href="https://github.com/Poojasonwane08/ebpf-autonomous-soc/blob/main/ebpf-threat-hunting-soc/docs/LIVE_EBPF_MODE.md">Live eBPF mode</a>).</p>
</blockquote>
<hr>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">What it does</h2><a id="user-content-what-it-does" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: What it does" href="https://github.com/Poojasonwane08/ebpf-autonomous-soc/tree/main/ebpf-threat-hunting-soc#what-it-does"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<markdown-accessiblity-table><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Capability</th>
<th>Implementation</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Kernel telemetry (eBPF)</td>
<td>Tetragon <code>process_exec</code> / <code>process_exit</code> / <code>process_kprobe</code> (tcp_connect, commit_creds, ptrace, memfd_create, security_file_permission). TracingPolicies in <code>deploy/tetragon/policies/</code>. Simulator emits the identical schema.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>High-throughput streaming</td>
<td><strong>Apache Kafka</strong> (KRaft) with 7 topics; ~20k events/s per engine core, horizontally scalable via consumer groups.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Syscall â†’ ATT&amp;CK schema</td>
<td>Declarative mapping <code>config/mitre_mapping.yml</code> (21 techniques, 12 tactics).</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Complex Event Processing</td>
<td><code>soc/detector.py</code> rebuilds <strong>process execution trees</strong> from disjoint kernel events, finds the attack root, groups alerts into incidents.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Lateral movement tracing</td>
<td>Joins <code>tcp_connect(:22)</code> on host A with <code>sshd â†’ shell</code> on host B and <strong>links the process trees across hosts</strong> into one incident.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Threat hunting rules</td>
<td><strong>15 Sigma rules</strong> (<code>rules/sigma/</code>) run by a built-in Sigma engine (modifiers, <code>1 of</code>, <code>not</code>, â€¦).</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Behavioural detection</td>
<td>Fileless malware (memfd_create â†’ exec from memory), ptrace memory injection, privilege escalation outside sudo/su.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Anomaly detection (ML)</td>
<td><strong>IsolationForest</strong> trained on a benign baseline (parent/child rarity, path, uid class, arg entropy, depth, spawn burst).</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>SOAR</td>
<td>5 YAML playbooks (<code>playbooks/</code>): freeze / kill process tree, isolate host, eBPF IP blocklist, evidence collection, webhook (n8n/Slack). Autonomous, monitor-only and analyst-approval modes.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Forensics</td>
<td>Automatic evidence bundle per incident: forensic timeline (JSON + Markdown), process trees, IOCs â†’ <code>evidence/INC-xxxx/</code>.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Adversary emulation</td>
<td>3 Caldera-style scenarios (<code>scenarios/</code>): APT with SSH lateral movement, fileless cryptominer, insider privilege escalation.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Dashboard</td>
<td>MITRE heatmap, fleet status, attack graph, process trees, alerts, SOAR actions, live telemetry, report.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
