<p dir="auto">GitHub Actions (<code>.github/workflows/ci.yml</code>) runs the tests on Ubuntu + Windows and an end-to-end test of the
full Docker/Kafka stack.</p>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Scope and limitations</h2><a id="user-content-scope-and-limitations" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Scope and limitations" href="https://github.com/Poojasonwane08/ebpf-autonomous-soc/tree/main/ebpf-threat-hunting-soc#scope-and-limitations"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">This is a practical, demonstrable version rather than an enterprise deployment:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>On Windows the eBPF sensors are <strong>simulated</strong> (same event format as Tetragon). Real eBPF runs only in
<a href="https://github.com/Poojasonwane08/ebpf-autonomous-soc/blob/main/ebpf-threat-hunting-soc/docs/LIVE_EBPF_MODE.md">Live mode</a> on Linux.</li>
<li>Live-mode remediation defaults to <strong>dry-run</strong>; isolation uses nftables and IP blocking uses a Tetragon
<code>Sigkill</code> TracingPolicy, both on the single host where the sensor runs.</li>
<li>The dashboard is custom (FastAPI + vanilla JS) instead of Kibana/Grafana to keep the stack light on a laptop;
all data is also on Kafka topics for Elasticsearch/Grafana ingestion.</li>
<li>State is in memory; restarting the dashboard clears it.</li>
</ul>
